`/test-catalog`, `/for-researchers` and `/honest-assessment` all said "0 tests discriminate from MOND+EFE+ΛCDM" while `/tier-1-existing` said of TEST-10 "this observable discriminates, and the framework loses it." TEST-09 separated the models at 3.3σ. Split into "0 could *select* Synchronism" vs "2 discriminated, both selecting MOND." Correcting upward is rarer here than downward, and the machinery wasn't set up for it.

